From dc1c88e367fc9054a61cc3123d83f5141f0a942d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:09:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] coreclr: build with GCC and libstdc++ (MinGW, ReactOS PSEH)

The MinGW build of patches 0009-0017 with UCRT64's GCC/binutils/libstdc++
instead of clang/lld/libc++.

- CMakeLists.txt: GCC's spellings of the MSVC options; /EHa is
  -fnon-call-exceptions. __try/__except/__finally come from ReactOS's PSEH
  (pseh2_64.h) with its gcc_plugin_seh (-fplugin), which CMake gets as
  CLR_MINGW_PSEH_INCLUDE and CLR_MINGW_GCC_SEH_PLUGIN.
  -fno-strict-aliasing: the Windows code type-puns as MSVC allows (cor.h
  reads a ULONG through uint32_t*; with strict aliasing GCC miscompiled
  CorSigUncompressData, which broke ildasm's signature decoding).
- ilasm, ildasm: link the metadata libraries as a group under MinGW
  (GNU ld resolves archives in one pass) and repeat utilcodestaticnohost
  after them in ilasm.
- inc/mingw/msvc_compat.h: libstdc++ spells try __try, so the SEH try
  statement is __seh_try { } __except (f) { } __endtry (PSEH needs the
  __endtry; with clang __seh_try is __try and __endtry is empty).
  GetExceptionCode()/GetExceptionInformation() stay names (members are
  called that) and are lambdas local to each filter. min/max are functions
  (libstdc++ undefines the macros); __assume, _ReturnAddress.
- palclr.h, palclr_win.h, jittelemetry.cpp, stacktrace.cpp: __seh_try and
  __endtry.
- controller.cpp, assembly.cpp, threads.cpp: the helpers that keep C++ EH
  out of a __try function are NOINLINE (gcc_plugin_seh rejects a function
  that has both, which GCC's inliner would otherwise create).
- utilcode.h: Interlocked*T overloads for GCC's NULL (__null, not an int).
- comtoclrcall.cpp: no static on definitions declared extern before.
- gc.cpp: GCC's _MM_HINT_T0 is an enumerator, not a macro.
- comcache.cpp: define CLSID_InProcFreeMarshaler rather than pull in the
  libuuid.a member that also has the IIDs <mtx.h> defines there.
---
